# The build context is this directory, and `COPY packages/ packages/` takes all of it. Whatever a working tree holds
# besides the sources -- installed modules, earlier builds, per-environment values files with credentials in them,
# test fixtures full of key-shaped strings -- would otherwise ride along into the image and in front of the scan that
# gates its publication. deploy/build.sh already leaves most of these out of its own tar; this file applies the same
# rule to every other way the image is built (CI, release-verify, a plain `docker build`).
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
deploy/values.*.env
packages/*/test
**/*.log
